NAME
       find - search for files in a directory tree

SYNOPSIS
       find [-H | -L | -P] [path...] [expression]

DESCRIPTION
       Walks each path depth first and evaluates the
       expression for every file. Tests: -name -iname -path
       -ipath -wholename -regex -iregex -type -size -empty
       -newer -anewer -cnewer -mtime -atime -ctime -mmin -amin
       -cmin -perm -user -group -uid -gid -nouser -nogroup
       -links -inum -samefile -readable -writable -executable
       -true -false. Options: -maxdepth -mindepth -depth -xdev
       -mount -daystart -regextype -follow -noleaf. Actions:
       -print -print0 -printf -fprint -ls -exec ... ; -exec
       ... {} + -execdir -delete -prune -quit. Operators: ( )
       ! -not -a -and -o -or , Without an action, -print is
       implied. -ok is not supported (no prompt).

NOTES
       -regex uses emacs syntax by default, as GNU find does,
       approximated through POSIX basic syntax. -exec ... +
       passes about 6 KB of arguments per command.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

